OL,3,GNEWSAHundreds in Chicago cheer on lone
OL,4,Amarathon runner
OL,5,
OL,6,FA runner who travelled 4,000 miles
OL,7,F(6,437km) to compete in a marathon was
OL,8,Fshocked and "lost for words" when
OL,9,Fhundreds of strangers were out on the
OL,10,Fstreets cheering him on and holding
OL,11,Fhomemade signs with his name on.
OL,13,FEthan Woodhead, 24, travelled from his
OL,14,Fhome in Guernsey to Chicago, in the US,
OL,15,Falone, expecting to complete Sunday's
OL,16,Frace without any friends or family
OL,17,Fsupporting him along the route.
OL,19,FUnknown to him, his uncle Phil Woodhead
OL,20,Fhad taken to Facebook to ask people in
OL,21,FChicago if they could surprise his
OL,22,Fnephew with a cheer as he ran past.
OL,23,APub: 14-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
